WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.420
The final trailer for Rogue One: A Star Wars
Story has arrived, and it finally pulls back

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.810
the curtain on exactly what fans can expect
from the franchise's first spinoff story.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.630
Just for you, we watched it 50 times and kept
our eyes peeled for things you might have

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.600
missed in the new Rogue One trailer...

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.650
Father-daughter story

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.020
With all the jump cuts and mood lighting,
you might have actually missed the central

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.181
thrust of the trailer, which is that the whole
thing really boils down to a father-daughter

00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:30.230
story, which is sort of familiar territory
for this whole Star Wars thing...

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.810
"Say you understand"

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:32.870
"I understand"

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.269
When Jyn's father Galen is seized by Stormtroopers,
she's left behind to fend for herself.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:42.260
But when the Rebels free her years later,
it turns out Dad is, in fact, working for

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.329
the Empire to create the Death Star.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:47.160
Can they stop the Death Star and save Daddy
at the same time?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.839
"We need to find him!"

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:50.399
We'll find out!

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:52.149
That's one big statue

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:57.059
Unlike the main Star Wars Saga films, Rogue
One is not expected to feature any Jedi in

00:00:57.059 --> 00:00:59.530
a meaningful way, Darth Vader excluded.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:05.360
Instead, this has been pitched as a story
of regular folks taking on the big, bad Empire.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.500
But this gorgeous shot of a U-Wing ship flying
over the remnants of a massive fallen Jedi

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.440
statue shows their influence is still part
of this larger world.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.600
Hmm....

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.550
Darth Vader looms large

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.990
Speaking of Darth Vader, the new footage here
finally shows him in action, suggesting he

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:23.430
may play a bigger role than previously expected.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.490
Could Vader's confrontation with Imperial
bad guy Director Krennic happen after the

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.310
Rebel team inflicts some damage on the Death
Star project?

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.360
Ship shape

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.100
We weren't sure until now what "Rogue One"
actually meant.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.780
Director Gareth Edwards had previously told
Empire magazine that the film's title was

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.240
more of a metaphor for the project itself,
as the first spinoff film not following known

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.980
characters like Luke, Leia, and the rest of
the gang.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:47.980
But on-screen?

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.820
We learn that it's also the impromptu call
sign they come up with for their ship during

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.820
the mission.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.800
"Rogue...Rogue One."

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.680
It feels more Hope-ful

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.040
It's no secret the film went back in for extensive
reshoots a few months before its December

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:07.250
2016 release date, with rumors swirling that
Disney wanted the film to look and feel more

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.649
upbeat and hopeful.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:10.879
"Take hold of this moment!"

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:15.159
And this attitude shows in the trailer, which
has a vibe much closer to that of the original

00:02:15.159 --> 00:02:16.900
Star Wars: A New Hope.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.700
Sure, it's an us-against-the-world story,
but the Rebels do still believe they can win.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.359
"Rebellions are built on hope!"

00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:27.349
The team goes undercover as Imperial officers

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:31.659
One fleeting shot shows Jyn and other members
of her Rebel strike team disguised as Imperial

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:32.730
officers.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.109
Could this be the moment where they first
break into the Imperial stronghold to find

00:02:36.109 --> 00:02:37.109
Galen?

00:02:37.109 --> 00:02:41.849
Also, for fans of the original trilogy, the
undercover move is a classic tactic to access

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:42.849
Empire facilities.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:45.050
"I can't see a thing in this helmet!"

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.050
Nice callback.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.670
"Aren't you a little short for a stormtrooper?"

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.670
"Huh?

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.769
Oh the uniform."

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:52.769
See Saw

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:57.769
Forest Whitaker is playing a mysterious man
who should be very familiar to fans of Star

00:02:57.769 --> 00:02:59.189
Wars: The Clone Wars...

00:02:59.189 --> 00:03:00.599
"Who are you?"

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:02.010
"I'm Saw Gerrera."

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:06.370
It's true: Whitaker has been confirmed as
Saw Gerrera, a rebel hero.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:11.040
Bringing in the character marks Star Wars'
first major crossover from the TV show to

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.109
film, and not the other way around.

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:16.279
Gerrera was introduced in The Clone Wars animated
series as a young man.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:20.980
Now, years later, Saw is all grown up and
live-action in Rogue One.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.220
Awesome.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.220
Alienation

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.769
It wouldn't be a Star Wars movie if we didn't
get to meet a few new alien species, but this

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:32.010
design certainly looks like it was pulled
from Mad Max: Fury Road director George Miller's

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.349
sketchbook.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:37.790
Despite the Immortan Joe vibe, though, this
alien named Edrio Two-Tubes is actually an

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.920
ally of Saw Gerrera.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.189
We're glad he's on our side...

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:42.189
Space Fights

00:03:42.189 --> 00:03:47.900
The Force Awakens was pretty great, but it
was lacking in one key area: space battles.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.059
That looks to change in Rogue One.

00:03:50.059 --> 00:03:54.549
The footage here shows a fleet of X-Wings
attacking a large Imperial ship in space.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:03:58.849
Finally: Rogue One is putting the star wars
back in Star Wars.

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:00.609
Birth of the Rebellion

00:04:00.609 --> 00:04:04.769
The Rebel planning scenes like the one here
echo the feel of the original trilogy, and

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:05.769
for good reason.

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:09.439
Before the Rebellion took the Empire head-on
in A New Hope, these disparate Rebel leaders

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:12.719
were figuring out how to join forces for their
first major mission.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:16.910
In other words, we're finally bearing witness
to the birth of the Rebellion as we first

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:17.910
knew it.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.680
"Make 10 men feel like a hundred"

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.720
Thanks for watching!

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.220
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.940
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you think of the Rogue One trailer...

